{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ages of three students are consecutive integers. Their mean (average) age is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. A fourth student joins the group and the mean of their four ages is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. How old is the fourth student?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a04c6e45595a61f7fc94317f85c7cf4030976d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 18\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 14\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the first 3 children be x, y, and z years old. The average then is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e1aa86e96dd6c8913de13afef6199d1141497f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y+z}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> so, if we multiply both sides by 3 we have x+y+z = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Now let the fourth student be w years old, the new average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/1369e9f5b3376da7d0124b80ae1d46046735d094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y+z+w}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. And if we multiply both sides by 4 we have x+y+z+w = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>So x+y+z+w = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and x+y+z = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, that means (x+y+z)+w = (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />)+w = 56 so w =<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e14394a336c0155b135d64aac8a08c6ff436198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E)}\\ 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~any1sgame\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the fourth student would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> years older than the average of the other three students because the average increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when the fourth student was added and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students in total, so the fourth student would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462a81c0c475a3b8892b62685e25198c7cb7dd22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> years older since it would be the same effect as if the fourth student was the same age as the average of the other three students and then all of their ages were increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the fourth student is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/1852a6b2c00588056c097200006bf79196a93899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 + 4 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"139\" height=\"30\" /> years old.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gau